// How the creatures' and characters' frames are sharpened, and how their edges are drawn, by animation package, size
// and body. The render style's Mobile Sharpening Scale (Shading Controls; `mobile_sharpening` in the shader presets,
// 1 in every style) multiplies the `sharpening` given here; the edge properties take no multiplier. Dynamapper reads
// your copy, cache/runtime_specs/mobiles/Sharpening.kdl beside the assets folder, in place of this file when it exists:
// copy this file there and edit the copy. Saving either file applies it within a second; a file that does not read
// leaves the table in force, with a warning naming the line, until it is fixed.
//
//   classic { ... }   the Classic animation package's frames
//   enhanced { ... }  the Enhanced animation package's frames (KR-like and UOD-Painterly draw them too)
//
// Each section holds:
//   default <properties>
//     Every body of the package not in a size class below, and any body whose frames the package does not list.
//   size max=<side> <properties>
//     The bodies whose largest stored frame side (the larger of width and height over every frame of every action
//     and facing, at 1x) is <side> pixels or less and more than the next smaller class's. A body above every class
//     takes the default.
//   body <id> [<last id>] <properties>
//     The body of in-game id <id> (the server's, as a mobile's body is sent), or every id from <id> to <last id>.
//
// A property a body leaves out comes from its size class, then from the default, then is off. The properties:
//   sharpening=<0..1>         Contrast-adaptive sharpening (AMD FidelityFX CAS) on each frame's own texels: soft detail
//                             more than hard edges. 1 is CAS's strongest, 0.625 its weakest, 0 off.
//   fringe_sharpening=<0..1>  The share of the sharpening a partly transparent texel takes: the soft, anti-aliased rim
//                             of the Enhanced frames, which sharpened turns into blocky light and dark texels when
//                             zoomed. 1 (the default) sharpens it as the rest, 0 not at all.
//   alpha_contrast=<0..1>     Pulls the rim's partial alpha towards transparent or opaque about alpha_midpoint, so
//                             fewer half-transparent texels show: 0 (the default) leaves the alpha, 1 cuts it at the
//                             midpoint. Each frame is cut before two frames crossfade, so the blend stays soft.
//   alpha_midpoint=<0.05..0.95>  The alpha the contrast turns about (default 0.5): lower keeps more of the rim.
//   contour=<0..1>            Darkens the rim and the outermost opaque texels towards contour_color, as the Classic
//                             frames' dark outline: 0 (the default) off, 1 the colour itself at the silhouette.
//   contour_color="#rrggbb"   The contour's and the outline's colour (default "#202020").
//   outline=<0..1>            A line of contour_color one texel wide outside the silhouette, at this opacity: 0 (the
//                             default) off. The frames are stored cropped to their visible pixels, so an outlined
//                             card grows by a texel each side.
//
// Classic frames are pixel art with a dark outline and no rim. The user, 2026-11-26, from clips at scale 0, 1 and 2:
// scale 1 is more faithful to the Classic art than 2, and the sharpening helps the larger Classic bodies even more
// than the small ones, so every Classic size takes the small bodies' 0.7 (the orc CAS's strongest). The Enhanced
// frames are rendered art with an anti-aliased rim; the Enhanced monsters look better at scale 2 than at 1, so their
// values are twice the first ones, while the Enhanced humans, elves and gargoyles keep the first values (0.4).

classic {
    default sharpening=0.7
    size max=96 sharpening=0.7
    size max=192 sharpening=0.7
    size max=384 sharpening=0.7
    // The orc: its pixel art takes CAS's strongest without grain.
    body 17 sharpening=1.0
}

enhanced {
    default sharpening=0.4
    size max=96 sharpening=1.0
    size max=192 sharpening=0.8
    size max=384 sharpening=0.6
    // The humans and their ghosts, the elves and the gargoyles: the monsters' values look too strong on them.
    body 400 403 sharpening=0.4
    body 605 606 sharpening=0.4
    body 666 667 sharpening=0.4
}
